{
 "rig": "Art/wharfIsoRig.js",
 "exposes": "globalThis.WharfIso",
 "contract": {
  "unit": "32 px = 1 m",
  "camera": "3/4, 45deg steps, elev 40deg (shared with the fleet, houses, characters)",
  "origin": "ground-centre of the footprint at CHART DATUM (z = 0 = lowest water)",
  "axes": "+X along the wharf run, +Y toward open water (the working face), +Z up",
  "cell": "sized from the projected bbox per call; render() returns {data,w,h,px,py,wet} where px,py is the projection of the origin",
  "water": "ZERO water pixels are baked. render().wet is a per-pixel mask of structure currently below the waterline; the shader owns the sea. opts.clipBelowWater drops those pixels.",
  "tide": "opts.tide = metres above datum, continuous. opts.tideRange = metres datum to HHW (0.3 - 14). Growth bands are pinned to the tidal FRAME, not to the water level.",
  "modularity": "bays x bayLen along X, width across Y. gameplay().snap gives -X / +X sockets at deck height for chaining modules.",
  "gangway": "run 3-14 m, height free. A float with gangway:true solves the ramp from ITS OWN rocked deck height each frame: the hinge and abutment are fixed, the landing rides the float. Guide piles, chain, anchor block and the solved ramp are tagged fixed and skipped by the rock transform."
 },
